// expect: 42
// Named-generic monomorphization, face 5 — a lambda BORN INSIDE a generic
// body. The lambda inherits the parent's vars, so it twins under the same
// instantiation: the parent's demand contributes every record nested in its
// body, and the closure-mint arm redirects the record's table index to the
// nested twin via the bracket's active enc (spec_closure_name) — captures,
// self-binding, and local naming keep the original name. Landing this also
// forced the width-consistency fix in find_local_handle_expr: a param used
// ONLY inside a nested lambda had no param-decl width source (the walk
// stopped at the closure boundary) while the capture-store read the live
// handle — $k i32 declared, $k.f64 read, an assembly break. Captures and
// evs are PARENT-frame expressions; the walk now reads them. RED (run 1,
// silent-wrong) on the pre-fix boot.
fn scale_all(xs, k) = map((x) => x * k, xs)

fn main() = {
  let ys = scale_all([1.5, 2.5], 2.0)
  if ys[0] == 3.0 && ys[1] == 5.0 { 42 } else { 1 }
}
